My approach:-
1. I initiated a unordered map 
2. I traverse the given array and from index 0 and store that in unordered map
3. if the next value's frequency in unordered map value is > k then we try to trim the map from left side and decrease the count. the count increase only if the frequency is greater than k.
4.And if count increase we parallely trying to figure out maximum count;
5. return maxcount;

Time complexity: O(N)
Space complexity: O(N)

My code:-
class Solution {
public:
    int maxSubarrayLength(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        int count = 0;
        int left = 0;
        int maxcount = 0;
        unordered_map<int,int> mpp;
        for(int i=0;i<nums.size();i++){
            mpp[nums[i]]++;
            // trimming from left

            while(mpp[nums[i]] > k){
                mpp[nums[left]]--;
                left++;
            }
           // length of max sub array 

            int count = i - left + 1;
            maxcount = max(maxcount, count);
        }
        return maxcount;
    }
};